---
number: 541
title: Hear the Pennies Dropping
author: Fidelia H. DeWitt
composer: William J. Kirkpatrick
sp_category: "35"
topic: Tithes and Offerings
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Hear the pennies dropping!
Listen while they fall;
Ev’ry one for Jesus,
He will get them all.

[chorus]
Dropping, dropping,
Dropping, dropping;
Hear the pennies fall!
Ev’ry one for Jesus,
He will get them all.

[verse 2]
Dropping, dropping ever,
From each little hand;
’Tis our gift to Jesus,
From His little band.

[chorus]
Dropping, dropping,
Dropping, dropping;
Hear the pennies fall!
Ev’ry one for Jesus,
He will get them all.

[verse 3]
Now, while we are little,
Pennies are our store;
But, when we are older,
Lord, we’ll give Thee more.

[chorus]
Dropping, dropping,
Dropping, dropping;
Hear the pennies fall!
Ev’ry one for Jesus,
He will get them all.

[verse 4]
Tho’ we’ve little money,
We can give Him love;
He will own our offering,
Smiling from above.

[chorus]
Dropping, dropping,
Dropping, dropping;
Hear the pennies fall!
Ev’ry one for Jesus,
He will get them all.
